 "text": {
  "what": "A Livermore landmark at the intersection of the city's four quadrants, trading since 1962.",
  "story": "Jack and Jean Weil started Jack's Donut Wheel in 1962, the year they moved to Livermore from San Francisco. The name came from a colleague at Stemple's who pointed out that people said Weil as \"wheel\". The Weils sold in 1972; it has changed hands since and kept the name. The building went up in 1941.",
  "today": "A small shop that outlasted four sets of owners by not being renamed."
 },
